{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2k57supprpkj6us7j5lzddkqmqvw5vngmmzwnx3yaut5ozb4ugtq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass, and the Rust translation required no changes — but the test harness did, twice.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/src/driver.c` is one 66-line translation unit: `printLine(const char*)`, `bad()`, `good()`, `driver()` exported, plus two `static` helpers. All functions are `void` and communicate only via `stdout`.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (mechanically derived)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D` on both `.so`s: `bad`, `driver`, `good`, `printLine`. Diff is **empty**; both correctly keep `helperBad`/`helperGood` local. No C module was skipped, so no symbol needed translating or stubbing. Verified for debug *and* release.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — grepping every rejection construct found exactly **one** conditional in the whole library (`if (line != NULL)`); no asserts, error enums, `return -1`, range checks, or `#ifdef`. 9 rows + 7 generic FFI-boundary rows (incl. G5, which documents *why* out-of-range-enum testing is inapplicable: the API has no enum or integer parameters — asserted mechanically so the premise can't rot).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — Cargo.toml has **no `[features]`**, CMakeLists has no options ⇒ exactly **1** feature combination. 20 rows across the axes the C actually distinguishes (all 4 entry points × input shapes × call sequences).\n\n## Phases B–D — results\n36 differential cases, all loading **both** `.so`s via `libloading` and comparing captured `stdout` byte-for-byte: 19 valid-path + 12 error-path + 5 symbol-parity. Green under `{}`, default, `--all-features`, and the release profile. Zero divergences in `src/lib.rs` (md5 unchanged).\n\n## Two harness bugs that would have made the suite lie\n1. **The suite was vacuous.** `cargo test` builds test binaries but **does not rebuild a `cdylib`**, so tests were loading a `.so` from an earlier `cargo build`. `mutation_check.sh` exposed this immediately: **all 9 deliberately-broken translations passed.** Fixed — the harness now rebuilds the cdylib (matching profile/features via `DIFFTEST_BUILD_ARGS`) and *asserts* the `.so` is newer than `src/`, so staleness fails loudly. After the fix, **9/9 mutations detected** (dropped/inverted NULL guard, calling the dead `helperBad`, dropping `helperGood`, lost newline, banner typo, reordered `driver()`, lossy-UTF-8 `println!`, payload-as-format-string).\n2. **libtest polluted the captures.** Parallel test threads write `test ... ok` to fd 1 — the descriptor under capture — causing a bogus mismatch (`...%%H~\\nok`). Fixed with `harness = false` + a sequential runner reporting only on stderr.\n\nNotable C behaviors deliberately preserved and pinned by tests: `bad()` never calls `helperBad()` (dead code); `printLine(\"\")` prints a newline while `printLine(NULL)` prints nothing; payloads containing `%n`/`%s` are never interpreted as format strings. The C `.so` imports `puts` (GCC strength-reduces `printf(\"%s\\n\", …)`) while Rust uses `printf` — byte-identical output, confirmed across randomized inputs including all 255 byte values and 1 MiB payloads.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified (source md5s unchanged; only the `build/` output dir was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":494,"cache_read_input_tokens":107443,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":494,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3457f3ae-3d25-4323-89a0-60dc492e09c6","uuid":"cc2d358d-f043-4b00-82e9-dbe75f5c02ed","timestamp":"2026-08-18T19:55:36.555Z"}
